ody wash, hand soaps, body lotions, and body creams, as well as sanitizer and other products. It sells its products under the Bath & Body Works and other brand names through retail stores and e-commerce sites in the United States and Canada, as well as through international stores operated by partners under the franchise, license, and wholesale arrangements. The company was formerly known as L Brands, Inc. and changed its name to Bath & Body Works, Inc. in August 2021. Bath & Body Works, Inc. was founded in 1963 and is headquartered in Columbus, Ohio.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Daniel  Heaf | CEO & Director | Age 47 | Compensation: $1.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 9K people. Revenue per employee of $804K ranks in the top quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $95K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Bath & Body Works, Inc. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $4.3B market cap on $7.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years and -5% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 71% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 63-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, with gross margins sitting at 42%.","The business throws off $865M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 12 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.70\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 4.1\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 13.2% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 1.9\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.7% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 8% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 79% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 42% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Large open-market insider purchases (net $0.8M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","40 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Bath & Body Works (NYSE:BBWI) Price Target Raised to $22.00","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/bath-body-works-nysebbwi-price-target-raised-to-22-00.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794589283.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Bath & Body Works (NYSE:BBWI) vs. Uxin (NASDAQ:UXIN) Head to Head Contrast","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/bath-body-works-nysebbwi-vs-uxin-nasdaquxin-head-to-head-contrast.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794582917.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.924,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Bath & Body Works (BBWI) Expected to Beat Earnings Estimates: What to Know Ahead of Q3 Release","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3028735/bath-body-works-bbwi-expected-to-beat-earnings-estimates-what-to-know-ahead-of-q3-release?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_9-3028735","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794492003.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Is Bath & Body Works (NYSE:BBWI) Widening Its Ulta Tie-Up?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/retail/is-bath-body-works-nysebbwi-widening-its-ulta-tie-up","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794403080.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.649,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"How (BBWI) Movements Inform Risk Allocation Models","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_relea